## Date ranges

In your response, you may include a starts_at and ends_at date range for each query if the topic or directions indicate a specific time period.

IMPORTANT: Today's date is {{ today() }}. The current year is {{ today().year }}. Use this as your reference point for all date calculations.

- Reference Point: Calculate all relative dates based on today's date: {{ today() }}.
- Format: Return timestamps in ISO 8601 format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.
- Boundaries: Start of day is 00:00:00 and End of day is 23:59:59.
- Default Year: If a month or quarter is specified without a year, use {{ today().year }}.
- Absence: If no date range is specified, do not include starts_at or ends_at fields.

Relative Date Logic

- "today" → starts_at: Current Date T00:00:00, ends_at: Current Date T23:59:59
- "yesterday" → starts_at: Previous Date T00:00:00, ends_at: Previous Date T23:59:59
- "this week" → starts_at: Monday of current week, ends_at: Sunday of current week
- "last week" → starts_at: Monday of previous week, ends_at: Sunday of previous week
- "this month" → starts_at: Day 1 of current month, ends_at: Last day of current month
- "last month" → starts_at: Day 1 of previous month, ends_at: Last day of previous month
- "this year" → starts_at: Jan 1 of current year, ends_at: Dec 31 of current year
- "recently", "lately", or vague time → starts_at: (Current Date - 30 days), ends_at: Current Date

Business Date Ranges
- "Q1" / "first quarter" → Jan 1 to Mar 31
- "Q2" / "second quarter" → Apr 1 to June 30
- "Q3" / "third quarter" → July 1 to Sept 30
- "Q4" / "fourth quarter" → Oct 1 to Dec 31
- "H1" / "first half" → Jan 1 to June 30
- "H2" / "second half" → July 1 to Dec 31

Note: Apply the current year ({{ today().year }}) unless a specific year is mentioned.

Examples (using today's date {{ today() }}):
Query: "Q3 sales targets"
terms: "sales targets", starts_at: "{{ today().year }}-07-01T00:00:00", ends_at: "{{ today().year }}-09-30T23:59:59"

Query: "last month's revenue"
terms: "revenue", starts_at: "{{ (today().replace(day=1) - timedelta(days=1)).replace(day=1).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT00:00:00') }}", ends_at: "{{ (today().replace(day=1) - timedelta(days=1)).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT23:59:59') }}"

Query: "Q4 2023 results"
terms: "results", starts_at: "2023-10-01T00:00:00", ends_at: "2023-12-31T23:59:59"

